// The original Python provider owns these nonserializable clients and views.
// These are descriptive signatures, not generated operations or live handles.
// SetupReviewRead, ReviewedSetupScopeInputs, ReviewedSetupApplyInputs,
// SetupScopeContinuation, SetupScopeCompletion, SetupCommandOutcome,
// SetupEvidenceRead and SetupReviewFailure deliberately have no wire identity.
// Do not synthesize them from detached records or replace the provider ports.
//
// WorkspaceSetupReviewClient.filesystem(repository_root, evidence_root,
//     execution_id, authority_manifest_locator) -> WorkspaceSetupReviewClient
// preview_review(request, scope_continuation=None) -> SetupReviewRead
// read_review(reference, expected_target, purpose) -> SetupReviewRead
// record_review_decision(reference, decision)
//     -> ReviewedSetupScopeInputs | ReviewedSetupApplyInputs
// record_scope_outcome(scope_inputs, outcome) -> SetupScopeCompletion
// apply_reviewed(inputs, client_intent_id) -> SetupCommandOutcome
// read_evidence(reference, expected_target) -> SetupEvidenceRead
// observe_action_admission(request: SetupActionAdmissionRequest)
//     -> SetupActionAdmissionObservation (nonwire, original read results only)
// release_client() -> SetupReviewClientCleanup
//
// ScopeOutcome is the original IssueMutationResult | IssueMutationError |
// SetupUnknownScopeOutcome. The nonwire completion retains the exact original
// return; its stored counterpart is SetupScopeOutcomeRecord and exact chunks.
// No alternate Json, nullable-success surrogate, copied physical schema or
// reconstructed admission is used to represent that union.
//
// SetupActionAdmissionObservation has no wire identity and cannot become a
// live apply input. Its exact Python view fields are target, action, review_ref,
// intent_ref, inputs_ref, review, intent, inputs, observation,
// product_dispatch_this_observation, historical_driver_outcome,
// private_observation, reads and authorizes_retry. Constants are respectively
// validated_retained_intent, not_invoked, not_established and false. Actual
// cleanup remains the separate original release_client result. This operation
// observes exact supplied historical references; it never discovers a record,
// refreshes currentness, writes intent or establishes driver completion.
